description:
Ship a `prospectus` command (Python, depends on a pinned `cli-login`).

Commands:
- `login --remote [--as EMAIL] [--note TEXT]`;
- `status` (the local session, no tokens);
- `whoami` (asks the server);
- `logout` (removes the session and revokes the refresh token);
- at least one CRM read through the Kanbus API that proves board access, for example listing the prospectus board's open issues.

The CLI finds everything from `https://prospectus.anth.us/cli/discovery`. Sessions use cli-login's store order: Keychain, Secret Service, kernel keyring, then the memory agent (`python -m cli_login.stores.agent serve --namespace prospectus --background`), then Windows. Never plain text.

API calls send `Authorization: Bearer`. Check which token the Kanbus API's authorizer accepts (access or ID) and whether workspace membership is still required. Signing in grants no CRM access by itself.

Specs inject a fake HTTP client and store; no network or credentials. Follow `cli.py` and `cli_test.py` in Decision-Flywheel.

Done when: the command installs from the repo and every subcommand has specs. Further CRM commands are separate stories.
